= Solution
{parent=iii}

The integrand defining $\varepsilon(t)$ is nonnegative by the <dominant energy condition>, hence
$$
\boxed{\varepsilon(t)\geq0}.
$$
Apply the spacetime <divergence theorem> to $J^a=T^{ab}V_b$ on the slab $S$. The flux through the cylinder at $r\to\infty$ vanishes by the stated decay. With the Lorentzian boundary orientation, the two spacelike boundary contributions give
$$
\varepsilon(t_0)-\varepsilon(t_1)
=\int_S\nabla_aJ^a\,d\operatorname{vol}_g.
$$
Part (ii) makes the right-hand side nonnegative, so for $t_1\geq t_0$,
$$
\boxed{\varepsilon(t_1)\leq\varepsilon(t_0)}.
$$
Therefore $\varepsilon$ is a nonnegative monotone decreasing energy functional.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

