The <curvature 2-forms> show that orthonormal curvature components grow as $m/r^3$. The <geodesic deviation> equation converts them into the relative acceleration of nearby parts of an observer. As $r\to0$, the <Schwarzschild tidal force> stretches radial separations and compresses transverse separations with unbounded magnitude. An extended body therefore undergoes destructive tidal deformation before reaching the <Schwarzschild singularity>.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.
